# Template: Front-End Advanced

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides an advanced template for complex front-end feature requirements in the PolygonExpress project. It focuses solely on giving structure to the initial requirements.md file for sophisticated front-end features.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
create-template: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/template-advanced.mdc
```

## Requirements Template

When this template is applied, it will create the following structure in requirements.md:

```markdown
# Complex Feature Requirements

## Objective
[What is the purpose of this feature?]

## Functional Requirements
[What functionality should this feature provide?]

## Component Architecture
[What components make up this feature and how do they interact?]

## State Management
[How should state be managed across components?]

## API Integration
[What API endpoints will this feature interact with?]

Endpoints:
- [Endpoint 1]: [Purpose and data format]
- [Endpoint 2]: [Purpose and data format]
- [Endpoint 3]: [Purpose and data format]

## Performance Requirements
[What performance metrics should this feature meet?]

## Accessibility Requirements
[What accessibility standards should this feature comply with?]

## Browser/Device Compatibility
[What browsers and devices should this feature support?]

## Dependencies
[What external libraries or existing components does this feature depend on?]

## User Experience Requirements
[What specific user experience considerations are important?]

## Edge Cases
[What edge cases need to be handled?]

## Success Criteria
[How will we know this feature is implemented correctly?]
```

## Template Application

When the template is applied, I will:
1. Create or update requirements.md with this template
2. Leave all sections empty for completion
3. Wait for the requirements to be completed before proceeding with any planning

## Next Steps
1. Complete the requirements template with feature details
2. Once requirements are complete, proceed with planning the implementation approach

## Use Cases
- Complex interactive features
- Multi-component systems
- Features with sophisticated state management
- API-intensive features
- Performance-critical implementations
- Accessibility-focused features 